From 5ff5dc92c62846ad48d6d322f9619c45c67b4551 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tesseract XRT port <jwkim@limagin.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:10:50 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 03/19] xocl/ulite: transmit from tty_port::xmit_fifo (Linux
 6.10)

Mainline commit 1788cf6a91d9 ("tty: serial: switch from circ_buf to
kfifo", v6.10) replaced uart_state::xmit (struct circ_buf) with the
kfifo tty_port::xmit_fifo and removed uart_circ_empty() and
uart_circ_chars_pending(). ulite_transmit() open-codes the circ_buf
tail handling and no longer compiles.

Guard: LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6, 10, 0) keeps the original
code; 6.10+ uses the kfifo. The boundary was checked against mainline
<linux/serial_core.h> (v6.9 has uart_state::xmit, v6.10 has
tty_port::xmit_fifo) and against the 6.17.0-35 and 7.0.0-x headers.

Equivalence, per step of the old code:
 - uart_circ_empty(xmit)          -> kfifo_is_empty(&tport->xmit_fifo)
 - send xmit->buf[tail], tail++   -> kfifo_get() one byte, send it
 - uart_circ_chars_pending(xmit)  -> kfifo_len(&tport->xmit_fifo)
circ_buf::buf was "char *", and kbuild compiles with -funsigned-char
(commit 3bc753c06dd0 "kbuild: treat char as always unsigned", v6.2;
present in the 6.8.0-147, 6.17.0-35 and 7.0.0-x Makefiles), so the old
byte was zero-extended into uart_out32()'s u32 argument, exactly as the
u8 from kfifo_get() is now: the value written to ULITE_TX is the same
for every byte, 0x80-0xff included, and no cast is needed (mainline
uartlite.c passes the u8 directly too).

ulite_transmit() is only called with port->lock held (ulite_worker()
and the serial core's start_tx), so kfifo_get() cannot fail after the
emptiness check; its result is still checked because it is
__must_check. icount.tx and the wake-up threshold are handled exactly
as before.

Upstream: based on the ulite.c part of XRT commit 04350f685, which
returns early when the popped byte is 0 ("if (ch <= 0)"), silently
dropping NUL bytes from the console stream; this patch does not.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SpY5QiU1d7kAe8YJM35EvA
---
 driver/xocl/subdev/ulite.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/driver/xocl/subdev/ulite.c b/driver/xocl/subdev/ulite.c
index 2111687..c2904a1 100644
--- a/driver/xocl/subdev/ulite.c
+++ b/driver/xocl/subdev/ulite.c
@@ -188,7 +188,13 @@ static int ulite_receive(struct uart_port *port, int stat)
 
 static int ulite_transmit(struct uart_port *port, int stat)
 {
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6, 10, 0)
 	struct circ_buf *xmit  = &port->state->xmit;
+#else
+	/* Linux 6.10 (commit 1788cf6a91d9) moved the TX buffer to a kfifo */
+	struct tty_port *tport = &port->state->port;
+	u8 ch;
+#endif
 
 	if (stat & ULITE_STATUS_TXFULL)
 		return 0;
@@ -200,15 +206,30 @@ static int ulite_transmit(struct uart_port *port, int stat)
 		return 1;
 	}
 
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6, 10, 0)
 	if (uart_circ_empty(xmit) || uart_tx_stopped(port))
 		return 0;
 
 	uart_out32(xmit->buf[xmit->tail], ULITE_TX, port);
 	xmit->tail = (xmit->tail + 1) & (UART_XMIT_SIZE-1);
+#else
+	if (kfifo_is_empty(&tport->xmit_fifo) || uart_tx_stopped(port))
+		return 0;
+
+	/* cannot fail: the fifo is not empty and port->lock is held */
+	if (!kfifo_get(&tport->xmit_fifo, &ch))
+		return 0;
+	/* same value as the old char read: kbuild uses -funsigned-char */
+	uart_out32(ch, ULITE_TX, port);
+#endif
 	port->icount.tx++;
 
 	/* wake up */
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6, 10, 0)
 	if (uart_circ_chars_pending(xmit) < WAKEUP_CHARS)
+#else
+	if (kfifo_len(&tport->xmit_fifo) < WAKEUP_CHARS)
+#endif
 		uart_write_wakeup(port);
 
 	return 1;
